BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:amorgos-kato-meria-kolofana-arkesini-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kato-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270727
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi\, Kato Meria
LOCATION:Kato Meria (Kolofana / Arkesini)\, Amorgos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The biggest panigiri on Amorgos and one of the biggest in the Cyclades: at the church of Agia Paraskevi in the south of the island\, the Kato Meria villages spend ten days preparing\, slaughter around 150 goats\, and on the evening of 25 July the patatato starts cooking in cauldrons for about 4\,000 people who eat free at long tables on the 26th and dance to violins until morning. Bring a car or arrange a lift from Katapola\; there is no bus back at 4 a.m.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#kato-meria-kolofana-arkesini-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kato
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#kato-meria-kolofana-arkesini-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kato
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:amorgos-kato-meria-kolofana-arkesini-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kato-2028@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20280725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20280727
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi\, Kato Meria
LOCATION:Kato Meria (Kolofana / Arkesini)\, Amorgos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The biggest panigiri on Amorgos and one of the biggest in the Cyclades: at the church of Agia Paraskevi in the south of the island\, the Kato Meria villages spend ten days preparing\, slaughter around 150 goats\, and on the evening of 25 July the patatato starts cooking in cauldrons for about 4\,000 people who eat free at long tables on the 26th and dance to violins until morning. Bring a car or arrange a lift from Katapola\; there is no bus back at 4 a.m.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#kato-meria-kolofana-arkesini-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kato
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#kato-meria-kolofana-arkesini-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kato
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:amorgos-katapola-psimeni-raki-festival-katapola-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270726
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270727
SUMMARY:Psimeni Raki Festival\, Katapola
LOCATION:Katapola\, Amorgos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 26 July the harbour square of Katapola celebrates the island's honey-and-spice raki: you watch it being made\, a boat arrives with dancers in costume\, the musicians meet them on the quay\, and everyone is handed psimeni raki\, pasteli and anevates (raki cheese pies) before the dancing goes on into the small hours. It clashes with the Agia Paraskevi feast the same night\, so locals pick one\; Katapola is the easier one without a car.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#katapola-psimeni-raki-festival-katapola
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#katapola-psimeni-raki-festival-katapola
END:VEVENT
